<title>UK: TABLE-UK's FTSE 100 top 10 post Grand Met.</title>
<headline>TABLE-UK's FTSE 100 top 10 post Grand Met.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The proposed merger between Grand Metropolitan Plc and Guinness Plc, announced on Monday, would create the eighth largest listed British company, according to data from Reuters Securities 3000.</p>
<p>Provided the merger is approved, the top 10 shares, in terms of market capitalisation would be as follows:</p>
<p> Company			Market Cap(U.S. dollars billion)</p>
<p> 1. HSBC Holdings Plc		    76.40</p>
<p> 2. Glaxo Wellcome Plc		   69.20</p>
<p> 3. British Petroleum Plc		67.49</p>
<p> 4. Shell Transport &amp; Trading Co Plc 60.16  5. Lloyds TSB Group Plc		 53.93</p>
<p> 6. British Telecommunications Plc   46.54</p>
<p> 7. SmithKline Beecham Plc	     45.67</p>
<p> 8. GMG Brands(Guinness/GrandMet)    39.40</p>
<p> 9. Barclays Plc			   30.87</p>
<p> 10.Zeneca Group Plc		     29.56</p>
<p>(Note: Market cap figures based on closing share prices on May 9. GMG Brands based on Guinness share price of 615p and Grand Met share price of 606p. One British pound = $1.62)</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
